WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.990 line:-1 align:center size:84%
The dashboard builds itself from any
dataset or SQL query.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.980 line:-1 align:center size:84%
The platform detects the metrics,
the dimensions and the time column,

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.040 line:-1 align:center size:84%
and decides what is worth showing.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.122 line:-1 align:center size:84%
Every indicator compares against the
previous month, against the same

00:00:17.122 --> 00:00:21.506 line:-1 align:center size:84%
month last year, and year to date
against the previous one. Green when

00:00:21.506 --> 00:00:23.260 line:-1 align:center size:84%
it grows, red when it falls.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.477 line:-1 align:center size:84%
And it respects the unit: amounts
vary in percent, and what already is

00:00:28.477 --> 00:00:31.040 line:-1 align:center size:84%
a percentage varies in percentage
points.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.030 line:-1 align:center size:84%
Filters recalculate everything:
indicators, series, bars and table.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:42.400 line:-1 align:center size:84%
The whole dashboard exports to Excel
or CSV with the filters applied, one

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.800 line:-1 align:center size:84%
sheet per chart.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.454 line:-1 align:center size:84%
And you can ask it in plain
language. It translates the question

00:00:47.454 --> 00:00:50.200 line:-1 align:center size:84%
into SQL, actually runs it against
the data and answers from the real

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.600 line:-1 align:center size:84%
result, not from memory.
